


-> @RestController vs @Controller

@Controller
    Used for MVC applications
    Returns HTML / JSP pages

    Example:-
        @Controller
        public class PageController {

            @GetMapping("/home")
            public String home() {
                return "home"; // view name
            }
        }

@RestController
        Used for REST APIs
        Returns JSON / XML
        Combines @Controller + @ResponseBody

        Example:-
            @RestController
            public class ApiController {

                @GetMapping("/hello")
                public String hello() {
                    return "Hello API";
                }
            }


-> In REST APIs → Always use @RestController
